corne-arcane-host (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Report the new revel scene for games and launchers. The firmware pairs it
    with the commons floor to select a district of its own, so a game no longer
    presents identically to a chat window. Older firmware rejects the value and
    falls back to showing the host as offline while such a window is focused;
    flash both halves before upgrading the daemon.
  * Background media no longer overrides the focused window. It supplies a
    scene only when no application profile matched, so a recognised window keeps
    its own presentation while something is playing. Two behaviours change: a
    document editor with media playing now reports its own scene rather than the
    archive scene, and so does a chat window.
  * Ship the X11 focus producer's user unit for sessions with no compositor
    focus bridge. It remains opt-in and is not enabled by installation.

 -- Griffin Hale <griffinhale.3@gmail.com>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 01:30:00 -0700

corne-arcane-host (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial Debian packaging of the optional host daemon. The install layout
    comes from host/Makefile, the same target host/package.nix drives, so the
    Debian and Nix installs cannot drift apart.
  * Ship 60-corne-arcane.rules for non-root access to the keyboard's Raw HID
    node. The number matters: systemd consumes the uaccess tag from a match in
    73-seat-late.rules, so a higher-numbered rule grants nothing.

 -- Griffin Hale <griffinhale.3@gmail.com>  Wed, 26 Aug 2026 19:38:39 -0700
